// The Long Grass Camp on the move (PRG-21, docs/design/moving-camp.md). The bedroll: sleep with the clan and walk the
// day with them to the next fire (<<camp walk>>). The ashes where the camp is not: gone on, or not come yet.

title: Camp_Bedroll
---
<<if not camp_ready()>>
    Bedroll: A clan bedroll, rolled tight. Nobody's walking tomorrow.
    <<stop>>
<<endif>>
Bedroll: The clan sleeps early. They walk at first light, all of them, children first.
-> Sleep, and walk with them.
    <<camp walk>>
-> Not yet.
    Bedroll: The fire keeps. So will they, till morning.
===

title: Camp_Ashes_Behind
---
<<if camp_site() >= 2>>
    Ashes: Cold. The grass is flattened on past the Gate, to the high grass.
<<else>>
    Ashes: Still warm. The grass is flattened east, toward the riverbed.
<<endif>>
===

title: Camp_Ashes_Ahead
---
Ashes: Old ashes in a ring of stones. Somebody camps here, some nights.
===
